OpenHarmony's clang sysroot has two conflicting definitions of
struct sockaddr_storage: sys/socket.h declares it (unless __MUSL__ is
set, which the OHOS target does not define) and the bionic-derived
linux/socket.h declares it unconditionally.  gnetworkmonitornetlink.c
includes both, so the translation unit fails to compile for the OHOS
target.

Skip linux/socket.h for that translation unit and provide the
__kernel_sa_family_t typedef it would have supplied.  linux/netlink.h
and linux/rtnetlink.h only need that typedef from linux/socket.h.

--- a/gio/gnetworkmonitornetlink.c
+++ b/gio/gnetworkmonitornetlink.c
@@ -38,6 +38,12 @@
 
 /* must come at the end to pick system includes from
  * gnetworkingprivate.h */
+#ifdef __OHOS__
+/* the OHOS sysroot's linux/socket.h redefines struct sockaddr_storage that
+ * sys/socket.h has already declared; skip it and keep the typedef below. */
+#define _UAPI_LINUX_SOCKET_H 1
+typedef unsigned short __kernel_sa_family_t;
+#endif
 #include <linux/netlink.h>
 #include <linux/rtnetlink.h>
 
